<!--
  Hub home — the primary app's index route (`/`).

  Top chrome: <ship-nav-top> (@ship/chrome) — the filled bar that composes
  the <sui-nav-top> primitive and assembles the ship-specific slot contents
  (brand mark, project switcher, breadcrumbs, theme picker, account menu,
  fullscreen). The page owns only the home content below the bar.

  note(deferred): hub root layout — layout convention gap. The intent was a
  single root layout (`<ship-nav-top>` once, wrapping every route). deck's
  bundler only discovers `routes/<subdir>/_layout.sui` (prefix `/<subdir>` —
  see crates/deck/deck-bundler/src/routes.rs::discover_layouts); a root
  `routes/_layout.sui` with prefix `/` (which would cover this index route) is
  never emitted. Emitting one needs a deck-engine change, which is out of this
  job's scope. Until then the nav is composed per-page (here + the studio
  route). Both render the same <ship-nav-top>.

  The `{name()}` binding exists so the compiler emits `hydrate` on the view's
  setup return (the compiler only emits hydrate when the template binds to
  scope signals; without it the runtime has nothing to call). The signal is a
  no-op constant.
-->
<ship-nav-top></ship-nav-top>
<main>
  <h1>{name()}</h1>
  <p>Ship's primary app — ready when you are.</p>
</main>
